				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-342026#post-2247080</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-342026/scp-7560-j#post-2247080</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Mar 2015 13:03:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>dankaar</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1790336</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The guy who runs TimeCube is, if not actually schizophrenic, puts up a good show of having classical symptoms of paranoid schizophrenia with delusions of grandeur<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-344039-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>. He's apparantly gone on record saying that he's been diagnosed with paranoid schizophrenia.</p> <p>That said, the question is if this -J is making fun of crackpot internet &quot;theories&quot;/those who make them in general, or people with Schizopherenia. I'm of the opinion that it's the former (as TimeCube is the most visible &quot;Internet Crackpot Theory&quot; rather than the most visible &quot;guy with schizophrenia&quot;), but I can see arguments for the latter.</p> <p><a href="http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Website/TimeCube?from=Main.TimeCube">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Website/TimeCube?from=Main.TimeCube</a></p> <p><a href="http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Cube">http://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Cube</a></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-344039-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Not sure if that last part is officially recognized, but when he outright states that he's better than god&#8230;</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
